      "body": "Profile model and thinking settings now act as defaults. Manual changes through Pi's model selector/cycling and thinking controls are retained per profile on the current session branch, across profile switches, resume/reload, and tree navigation. Earlier entries remain immutable. Agent definitions, other sessions, and delegated child settings remain unchanged.\n\nValidation: typecheck and all 17 tests passed, including a real offline SDK/child session. The installed global Pi resource loader loaded 21 extensions without errors. An actual `higgsfield-specialist` main profile activated with `openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol` and high thinking; a manual switch to `gpt-6-astra` and medium thinking survived reset/reactivation without inference requests. All ten packaged/installed files match source hashes.\n\nThe English specialist profile and explicit child native MCP entry point are saved separately in [Pi Home Kit](https://github.com/rodrigojager/pi-home-kit/tree/main/profiles/higgsfield-specialist). The original 36-skill Higgsfield library is shared under `~/.agents/skills/higgsfield` and was not modified. The official MCP connection was validated to `needs-auth`; OAuth sign-in is still required before service execution. No paid media generation was performed.\n\nActivate an already-open Pi with `/reload` after current work finishes. Select agents with Alt+A. Delegated children continue using their definition defaults.\n"
